Lumbre builds on work by others. None of it is copied into this repository;
each item is fetched at build time or installed and downloaded by the user.

- llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), MIT License. Lumbre runs
  its `llama-server` program as a worker process. Not bundled in 0.1.
- Nodalia Design Language (https://github.com/danielmigueltejedor/nodalia-design),
  MIT License. The desktop app takes its `nodalia-theme` crate as a dependency.
- Rust crates listed in Cargo.lock, under their own licences (checked in CI
  with cargo-deny against the allow-list in deny.toml).
- Model weights are not part of Lumbre. Each manifest in models/ names the
  publisher, the upstream model card, the pinned revision and the licence of
  the weights it points to. The built-in manifests point to Qwen models
  published by Alibaba Cloud under the Apache License 2.0.

- The application icons show Leonardo Torres Quevedo, from a 1921 autochrome
  by Auguste Léon (Archives de la Planète, Musée départemental Albert-Kahn),
  in the public domain. Source and processing: design/icon/SOURCE.md.

"Lumbre Nano", "Mini", "Lumbre" and "Lumbre Code" are names of size classes
(tiers), not of models trained by this project.
